,+2.9184e-01]\nh=  50 Delta_M2=-8.850786e-04 Delta_M1(sample)=-4.789852e-02 CI=[-1.8174e-01,+9.8747e-02]\nh= 100 Delta_M2=-2.783950e-03 Delta_M1(sample)=+3.783166e-02 CI=[-1.0238e-01,+1.7805e-01]\nt= 0.25 xi_peak=1.000 Imax=7.941884e-06 xi_rms=18.908 w=18.042 w/xi=18.042\nt= 1.00 xi_peak=1.000 Imax=7.771604e-05 xi_rms=18.907 w=18.041 w/xi=18.041\nt= 4.00 xi_peak=2.000 Imax=6.637221e-05 xi_rms=18.910 w=17.192 w/xi=8.596\n\n===============================================================================\nAUDIT COMPLETE\n===============================================================================\n\nGenerated:\n  quantum_classical_audit/memory_audit.csv\n  quantum_classical_audit/information_entanglement_audit.csv\n  quantum_classical_audit/information_profile_descriptors.csv\n  quantum_classical_audit/deterministic_collapse_audit.csv\n  quantum_classical_audit/AUDIT_SUMMARY.txt\n\nDeterministic collapse diagnostics:\n       scaling  mean_RMSE  max_RMSE  n_profiles\n     LA_over_N   0.000684  0.001683          15\n    LA_over_xi   0.000504  0.000756          15\ncentered_width   0.000557  0.000857          15\n\nImportant:\nA positive I(A:B) is not sufficient to claim entanglement.\nUse PPT_M2=False / nu_PT_min < 1/2 / positive log-negativity\nas the Gaussian entanglement criterion.\n\nDONE\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\n\"\"\"\n===============================================================================\nQUANTUM vs CLASSICAL MEMORY AUDIT — NON-STATIONARY TWO-TIME KERNEL\n===============================================================================\n\nPURPOSE\n-------\n\nReconstruct and audit, from scratch, a Gaussian quantum quench M2 and a\nclassical separable matched-kernel surrogate M1.\n\nThe crucial correction relative to the previous version is:\n\n    DO NOT ASSUME STATIONARITY AFTER THE QUENCH.\n\nTherefore we use the full two-time kernel\n\n    Gamma_ij =\n        1/2 < { H_Q(t_i), H_Q(t_j) } >\n\nrather than\n\n    Gamma_ij = C_H(|t_i-t_j|).\n\nFor the linear hidden observable\n\n    H_Q(t) = g^T q(t)\n\nand phase-space vector\n\n    X = (q,p),\n\nwe have\n\n    H_Q = h^T X\n\nwith\n\n    h = (g,0).\n\nThe exact Heisenberg propagation is\n\n    X(t) = S(t) X(0)\n\nand\n\n    S(t) = exp(A t),\n\nwhere\n\n    A = [[0, I],\n         [-K1,0]]\n\nwith\n\n    K1 = D + J0 J_base.\n\nInitial covariance:\n\n    V0 = 1/2 diag(D^(-1/2), D^(1/2))\n\nThe exact two-time symmetrized covariance is\n\n    Gamma_ij =\n        h^T [\n            S_i V0 S_j^T\n            +\n            S_j V0 S_i^T\n        ] h / 2.\n\nM1 is defined as a classical Gaussian process with exactly this same\nfinite-dimensional covariance matrix:\n\n    Gamma_M1 = Gamma_M2.\n\nTherefore the linear window variance must agree:\n\n    Var(Y_h) =\n        dt^2 1^T Gamma_h 1.\n\nThe purpose is NOT to claim that matching one scalar process makes the\nfull classical model equivalent to the quantum state.\n\nInstead we separately test:\n\n    1. two-time hidden-force statistics;\n    2. linear memory;\n    3. mutual information;\n    4. Gaussian PPT criterion;\n    5. logarithmic negativity.\n\nIMPORTANT\n---------\n\nMI > 0 is NOT sufficient to establish entanglement.\n\nFor a Gaussian state in hbar=1 units:\n\n    entanglement iff\n\n        nu_tilde_min < 1/2\n\nfor the partially transposed covariance.\n\nLogarithmic negativity:\n\n    E_N = sum_j max(0,-log(2 nu_tilde_j))\n\nusing the natural logarithm.\n\nM1 is a classical separable surrogate and therefore has:\n\n    I_M1 = 0\n    negativity_M1 = 0\n    log_negativity_M1 = 0\n\nby construction.\n\nRECONSTRUCTION ASSUMPTION\n-------------------------\n\nThe historical J_base matrix is not available in the present context.\n\nThe default reconstruction is therefore:\n\n    J_base = nearest-neighbour open-chain Laplacian.\n\nIf the original model used another J_base, replace ONLY make_J_base().\n\n===============================================================================\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport math\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Tuple, List, Dict\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom scipy.linalg import expm\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# CONFIGURATION\n# =============================================================================\n\n@dataclass\nclass Config:\n\n    # System sizes\n    N_values: Tuple[int, ...] = (\n        16,\n        24,\n        32,\n        48,\n        64,\n    )\n\n    # Quench strengths\n    J0_values: Tuple[float, ...] = (\n        0.001,\n        0.002,\n        0.004,\n    )\n\n    # Bare frequency matrix:\n    #\n    # D = omega0^2 I\n    #\n    omega0: float = 1.0\n\n    # Boundary condition for J_base\n    periodic_boundary: bool = False\n\n    # Hidden-force site\n    hidden_site: int = 0\n\n    # Time grid\n    dt: float = 0.02\n    t_max: float = 8.0\n\n    # Reference times used for information/entanglement\n    information_times: Tuple[float, ...] = (\n        0.25,\n        1.0,\n        4.0,\n    )\n\n    # Memory windows\n    memory_h_values: Tuple[int, ...] = (\n        10,\n        50,\n        100,\n    )\n\n    # Subsystem sizes\n    LA_values: Tuple[int, ...] = (\n        1,\n        2,\n        4,\n        8,\n    )\n\n    # Numerical tolerances\n    symplectic_tol: float = 1e-9\n    physicality_tol: float = 1e-9\n    ppt_tol: float = 1e-9\n\n    # Optional classical Monte Carlo\n    n_classical_samples: int = 400\n    n_bootstrap: int = 2000\n\n    random_seed: int = 20260916\n\n    output_dir: str = (\n        \"quantum_classical_audit_corrected\"\n    )\n\n\nCFG = Config()\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# BASIC UTILITIES\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef symmetrize(M: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    return 0.5 * (M + M.T)\n\n\ndef relative_rmse(\n    x: np.ndarray,\n    y: np.ndarray\n) -> Tuple[float, float, float]:\n\n    diff = x - y\n\n    rmse = float(\n        np.sqrt(np.mean(diff ** 2))\n    )\n\n    scale = float(\n        np.sqrt(np.mean(x ** 2))\n    )\n\n    rel = (\n        rmse / scale\n        if scale > 0\n        else np.nan\n    )\n\n    max_abs = float(\n        np.max(np.abs(diff))\n    )\n\n    return rmse, rel, max_abs\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# MODEL MATRICES\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef make_D(\n    N: int,\n    omega0: float\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    return (\n        omega0 ** 2\n    ) * np.eye(N)\n\n\ndef make_J_base(\n    N: int,\n    periodic: bool = False\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Default reconstructed coupling.\n\n    Open chain:\n\n        1 -1\n       -1  2 -1\n           ...\n           -1 2 -1\n              -1 1\n\n    This is the positive semidefinite nearest-neighbour Laplacian.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    J = np.zeros(\n        (N, N),\n        dtype=float\n    )\n\n    if N == 1:\n        return J\n\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n\n        J[i, i] += 1.0\n        J[i + 1, i + 1] += 1.0\n\n        J[i, i + 1] -= 1.0\n        J[i + 1, i] -= 1.0\n\n    if periodic and N > 2:\n\n        J[0, 0] += 1.0\n        J[-1, -1] += 1.0\n\n        J[0, -1] -= 1.0\n        J[-1, 0] -= 1.0\n\n    return symmetrize(J)\n\n\ndef make_model(\n    N: int,\n    J0: float,\n    cfg: Config\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n\n    D = make_D(\n        N,\n        cfg.omega0\n    )\n\n    J_base = make_J_base(\n        N,\n        cfg.periodic_boundary\n    )\n\n    K0 = D.copy()\n\n    K1 = (\n        D\n        +\n        J0 * J_base\n    )\n\n    return (\n        symmetrize(K0),\n        symmetrize(K1),\n        J_base,\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# MATRIX SQUARE ROOTS\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef matrix_sqrt(\n    M: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    M = symmetrize(M)\n\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(M)\n\n    if np.min(vals) <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"Matrix is not positive definite.\"\n        )\n\n    return symmetrize(\n        (vecs * np.sqrt(vals)) @ vecs.T\n    )\n\n\ndef matrix_inv_sqrt(\n    M: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    M = symmetrize(M)\n\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(M)\n\n    if np.min(vals) <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"Matrix is not positive definite.\"\n        )\n\n    return symmetrize(\n        (vecs * (1.0 / np.sqrt(vals)))\n        @ vecs.T\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# INITIAL QUANTUM COVARIANCE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef make_initial_covariance(\n    K0: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    N = K0.shape[0]\n\n    K0_inv_sqrt = matrix_inv_sqrt(\n        K0\n    )\n\n    K0_sqrt = matrix_sqrt(\n        K0\n    )\n\n    V0 = np.zeros(\n        (2 * N, 2 * N),\n        dtype=float\n    )\n\n    V0[:N, :N] = (\n        0.5 * K0_inv_sqrt\n    )\n\n    V0[N:, N:] = (\n        0.5 * K0_sqrt\n    )\n\n    return symmetrize(V0)\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# SYMPLECTIC FORM\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef symplectic_form(\n    N: int\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    I = np.eye(N)\n    Z = np.zeros(\n        (N, N)\n    )\n\n    return np.block([\n        [Z, I],\n        [-I, Z],\n    ])\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# DYNAMICS\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef dynamical_matrix(\n    K: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    N = K.shape[0]\n\n    Z = np.zeros(\n        (N, N)\n    )\n\n    I = np.eye(N)\n\n    return np.block([\n        [Z, I],\n        [-K, Z],\n    ])\n\n\ndef propagator(\n    K: np.ndarray,\n    t: float\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    A = dynamical_matrix(\n        K\n    )\n\n    return expm(\n        A * t\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PROPAGATOR TABLE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef make_time_grid(\n    cfg: Config\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    n = int(\n        round(\n            cfg.t_max / cfg.dt\n        )\n    )\n\n    return (\n        np.arange(n + 1)\n        * cfg.dt\n    )\n\n\ndef make_propagator_table(\n    K1: np.ndarray,\n    times: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns\n\n        S_table[i] = S(times[i])\n\n    shape:\n\n        (nt, 2N, 2N)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    return np.asarray([\n        propagator(\n            K1,\n            float(t)\n        )\n        for t in times\n    ])\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# SIMPLECTICITY AUDIT\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef symplectic_residual(\n    S: np.ndarray,\n    Omega: np.ndarray\n) -> float:\n\n    return float(\n        np.linalg.norm(\n            S @ Omega @ S.T\n            - Omega,\n            ord=np.inf\n        )\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# ROBUST SYMPLECTIC EIGENVALUES\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef symplectic_eigenvalues(\n    V: np.ndarray\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Robust numerical extraction of Gaussian symplectic eigenvalues.\n\n    For\n\n        M = i Omega V\n\n    the eigenvalues are approximately\n\n        +/- nu_j.\n\n    We sort absolute values and average adjacent pairs.\n\n    The result is forced to be real and non-negative.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    V = symmetrize(\n        np.real_if_close(V)\n    )\n\n    N = V.shape[0] // 2\n\n    Omega = symplectic_form(\n        N\n    )\n\n    eigvals = np.linalg.eigvals(\n        1j * Omega @ V\n    )\n\n    absvals = np.sort(\n        np.abs(\n            eigvals\n        )\n    )\n\n    if len(absvals) != 2 * N:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"Unexpected symplectic spectrum size.\"\n        )\n\n    # The spectrum is:\n    #\n    # nu_1, nu_1, nu_2, nu_2, ...\n    #\n    # after sorting by absolute value.\n    #\n    # Pair explicitly.\n    nus = 0.5 * (\n        absvals[0::2]\n        +\n        absvals[1::2]\n    )\n\n    nus = np.real_if_close(\n        nus\n    ).astype(float)\n\n    nus[nus < 0] = 0.0\n\n    return np.sort(\n        nus\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHYSICALITY\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef physicality_audit(\n    V: np.ndarray\n) -> Dict[str, float]:\n\n    nus = symplectic_eigenvalues(\n        V\n    )\n\n    nu_min = float(\n        np.min(nus)\n    )\n\n    nu_max = float(\n        np.max(nus)\n    )\n\n    return {\n        \"nu_min\": nu_min,\n        \"nu_max\": nu_max,\n        \"physicality_gap\": (\n            nu_min - 0.5\n        ),\n    }\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# GAUSSIAN ENTROPY\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef bosonic_entropy(\n    nu: float\n) -> float:\n\n    nu = float(\n        max(nu, 0.5)\n    )\n\n    n = nu - 0.5\n\n    if n <= 1e-15:\n        return 0.0\n\n    return float(\n        (n + 1.0)\n        * np.log(n + 1.0)\n        -\n        n * np.log(n)\n    )\n\n\ndef gaussian_entropy(\n    V: np.ndarray\n) -> float:\n\n    nus = symplectic_eigenvalues(\n        V\n    )\n\n    return float(\n        np.sum([\n            bosonic_entropy(nu)\n            for nu in nus\n        ])\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# SUBSYSTEM COVARIANCE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef phase_space_indices(\n    N: int,\n    sites: List[int]\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    sites = np.asarray(\n        sites,\n        dtype=int\n    )\n\n    return np.concatenate([\n        sites,\n        N + sites,\n    ])\n\n\ndef reduce_covariance(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    sites: List[int]\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    idx = phase_space_indices(\n        N,\n        sites\n    )\n\n    return symmetrize(\n        V[np.ix_(idx, idx)]\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# MUTUAL INFORMATION\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef mutual_information(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    sites_A: List[int]\n) -> float:\n\n    sites_A = list(\n        sites_A\n    )\n\n    sites_all = list(\n        range(N)\n    )\n\n    sites_B = [\n        i\n        for i in sites_all\n        if i not in sites_A\n    ]\n\n    VA = reduce_covariance(\n        V,\n        N,\n        sites_A\n    )\n\n    VB = reduce_covariance(\n        V,\n        N,\n        sites_B\n    )\n\n    SAB = gaussian_entropy(\n        V\n    )\n\n    SA = gaussian_entropy(\n        VA\n    )\n\n    SB = gaussian_entropy(\n        VB\n    )\n\n    I = (\n        SA\n        +\n        SB\n        -\n        SAB\n    )\n\n    # Numerical cleanup.\n    if abs(I) < 1e-12:\n        I = 0.0\n\n    return float(\n        max(I, 0.0)\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PARTIAL TRANSPOSE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef partial_transpose_covariance(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    sites_A: List[int]\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    Lambda = np.ones(\n        2 * N\n    )\n\n    for site in sites_A:\n\n        # q unchanged\n        # p -> -p\n        Lambda[\n            N + site\n        ] = -1.0\n\n    PT = np.diag(\n        Lambda\n    )\n\n    return symmetrize(\n        PT @ V @ PT\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PPT / NEGATIVITY\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef ppt_negativity(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    sites_A: List[int],\n    tol: float\n) -> Dict[str, float]:\n\n    Vpt = partial_transpose_covariance(\n        V,\n        N,\n        sites_A\n    )\n\n    nus_pt = symplectic_eigenvalues(\n        Vpt\n    )\n\n    nu_min = float(\n        np.min(nus_pt)\n    )\n\n    # PPT criterion\n    ppt = (\n        nu_min\n        >=\n        0.5 - tol\n    )\n\n    # Simple PPT violation measure\n    negativity = float(\n        np.sum(\n            np.maximum(\n                0.0,\n                0.5 - nus_pt\n            )\n        )\n    )\n\n    # Gaussian logarithmic negativity\n    log_negativity = float(\n        np.sum([\n            max(\n                0.0,\n                -np.log(\n                    2.0 * nu\n                )\n            )\n            for nu in nus_pt\n        ])\n    )\n\n    return {\n        \"PPT\": bool(ppt),\n        \"nu_PT_min\": nu_min,\n        \"negativity\": negativity,\n        \"log_negativity\": log_negativity,\n    }\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# HIDDEN OBSERVABLE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef hidden_vector(\n    N: int,\n    site: int\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    if site < 0 or site >= N:\n\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"hidden site {site} \"\n            f\"outside [0,{N-1}]\"\n        )\n\n    g = np.zeros(\n        N\n    )\n\n    g[site] = 1.0\n\n    return g\n\n\ndef hidden_phase_vector(\n    N: int,\n    site: int\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    g = hidden_vector(\n        N,\n        site\n    )\n\n    return np.concatenate([\n        g,\n        np.zeros(N),\n    ])\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# FULL NON-STATIONARY TWO-TIME KERNEL\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef full_two_time_kernel(\n    V0: np.ndarray,\n    S_table: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    hidden_site: int\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Full non-stationary kernel.\n\n    Gamma_ij =\n        1/2 < {H(t_i),H(t_j)} >\n\n    with\n\n        H(t) = h^T S(t) X(0).\n\n    Therefore\n\n        Gamma_ij =\n          1/2 h^T[\n             S_i V0 S_j^T\n             +\n             S_j V0 S_i^T\n          ]h.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    h = hidden_phase_vector(\n        N,\n        hidden_site\n    )\n\n    nt = len(\n        S_table\n    )\n\n    Gamma = np.zeros(\n        (nt, nt),\n        dtype=float\n    )\n\n    # Precompute h^T S_i\n    #\n    # This reduces the cost substantially:\n    #\n    # a_i = h^T S_i\n    #\n    # Gamma_ij =\n    #   a_i V0 a_j^T\n    #\n    A = np.asarray([\n        h @ S\n        for S in S_table\n    ])\n\n    # Since V0 is symmetric:\n    #\n    # a_i V0 a_j^T\n    #\n    # is already symmetric in i,j.\n    #\n    Gamma = (\n        A @ V0 @ A.T\n    )\n\n    Gamma = symmetrize(\n        Gamma\n    )\n\n    return Gamma\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# DIRECT TWO-TIME CHECK\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef direct_kernel_element(\n    V0: np.ndarray,\n    S_i: np.ndarray,\n    S_j: np.ndarray,\n    h: np.ndarray\n) -> float:\n\n    Cij = 0.5 * (\n        S_i @ V0 @ S_j.T\n        +\n        S_j @ V0 @ S_i.T\n    )\n\n    return float(\n        h @ Cij @ h\n    )\n\n\ndef validate_kernel_formula(\n    V0: np.ndarray,\n    S_table: np.ndarray,\n    Gamma: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    hidden_site: int,\n    rng: np.random.Generator,\n    n_tests: int = 20\n) -> float:\n\n    h = hidden_phase_vector(\n        N,\n        hidden_site\n    )\n\n    nt = len(\n        S_table\n    )\n\n    errors = []\n\n    for _ in range(\n        min(n_tests, nt * nt)\n    ):\n\n        i = int(\n            rng.integers(\n                0,\n                nt\n            )\n        )\n\n        j = int(\n            rng.integers(\n                0,\n                nt\n            )\n        )\n\n        direct = direct_kernel_element(\n            V0,\n            S_table[i],\n            S_table[j],\n            h\n        )\n\n        fast = Gamma[i, j]\n\n        errors.append(\n            abs(\n                direct - fast\n            )\n        )\n\n    return float(\n        max(errors)\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# M1 CLASSICAL MATCHED PROCESS\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef project_psd(\n    M: np.ndarray,\n    floor: float = 0.0\n) -> np.ndarray:\n\n    M = symmetrize(\n        M\n    )\n\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(\n        M\n    )\n\n    vals = np.maximum(\n        vals,\n        floor\n    )\n\n    return symmetrize(\n        (vecs * vals)\n        @ vecs.T\n    )\n\n\ndef sample_classical_process(\n    Gamma: np.ndarray,\n    n_samples: int,\n    rng: np.random.Generator\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Draw classical Gaussian trajectories:\n\n        x ~ N(0,Gamma)\n\n    Returns:\n\n        shape = (n_samples, nt)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    Gamma_psd = project_psd(\n        Gamma\n    )\n\n    vals, vecs = np.linalg.eigh(\n        Gamma_psd\n    )\n\n    vals = np.maximum(\n        vals,\n        0.0\n    )\n\n    sqrtGamma = (\n        vecs\n        * np.sqrt(vals)\n    ) @ vecs.T\n\n    Z = rng.normal(\n        size=(\n            n_samples,\n            Gamma.shape[0]\n        )\n    )\n\n    return (\n        Z @ sqrtGamma.T\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# MEMORY FROM FULL TWO-TIME KERNEL\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef window_variance_from_full_kernel(\n    Gamma: np.ndarray,\n    dt: float,\n    start: int,\n    h: int\n) -> float:\n\n    stop = start + h\n\n    if stop > Gamma.shape[0]:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"Memory window exceeds time grid.\"\n        )\n\n    G = Gamma[\n        start:stop,\n        start:stop\n    ]\n\n    ones = np.ones(\n        h\n    )\n\n    return float(\n        dt ** 2\n        * ones @ G @ ones\n    )\n\n\ndef window_reference_variance(\n    Gamma: np.ndarray,\n    dt: float,\n    h: int\n) -> float:\n\n    return window_variance_from_full_kernel(\n        Gamma,\n        dt,\n        start=0,\n        h=h\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# MEMORY AUDIT\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef memory_audit(\n    Gamma: np.ndarray,\n    dt: float,\n    h_values: Tuple[int, ...],\n    rng: np.random.Generator,\n    n_samples: int,\n    n_bootstrap: int\n) -> List[Dict]:\n\n    rows = []\n\n    for h in h_values:\n\n        if h > Gamma.shape[0]:\n            continue\n\n        # Exact M2 variance\n        V_M2 = window_reference_variance(\n            Gamma,\n            dt,\n            h\n        )\n\n        # M1 uses exactly the same Gamma\n        V_M1_theory = window_reference_variance(\n            Gamma,\n            dt,\n            h\n        )\n\n        Delta_M2 = (\n            V_M2 / V_M1_theory\n            - 1.0\n        )\n\n        Delta_M1_theory = (\n            V_M1_theory\n            / V_M2\n            - 1.0\n        )\n\n        # ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n        # Classical finite ensemble\n        # ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        G_h = Gamma[\n            :h,\n            :h\n        ]\n\n        classical_samples = sample_classical_process(\n            G_h,\n            n_samples,\n            rng\n        )\n\n        Y_M1 = (\n            dt\n            * np.sum(\n                classical_samples,\n                axis=1\n            )\n        )\n\n        sample_variance = float(\n            np.var(\n                Y_M1,\n                ddof=1\n            )\n        )\n\n        Delta_M1_sample = (\n            sample_variance\n            / V_M1_theory\n            - 1.0\n        )\n\n        # Bootstrap CI for the classical finite-sample estimator.\n        boot = np.empty(\n            n_bootstrap\n        )\n\n        for b in range(\n            n_bootstrap\n        ):\n\n            idx = rng.integers(\n                0,\n                n_samples,\n                size=n_samples\n            )\n\n            Yb = Y_M1[\n                idx\n            ]\n\n            vb = np.var(\n                Yb,\n                ddof=1\n            )\n\n            boot[b] = (\n                vb\n                / V_M1_theory\n                - 1.0\n            )\n\n        ci_low, ci_high = np.percentile(\n            boot,\n            [2.5, 97.5]\n        )\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"h\": h,\n            \"V_M2\": V_M2,\n            \"V_M1_theory\": V_M1_theory,\n            \"absolute_variance_difference\": (\n                V_M2\n                -\n                V_M1_theory\n            ),\n            \"relative_variance_difference\": (\n                (\n                    V_M2\n                    -\n                    V_M1_theory\n                )\n                / V_M2\n                if V_M2 != 0\n                else np.nan\n            ),\n            \"Delta_M2\": Delta_M2,\n            \"Delta_M1_theory\": Delta_M1_theory,\n            \"Delta_M1_sample\": Delta_M1_sample,\n            \"Delta_M1_CI_low\": float(\n                ci_low\n            ),\n            \"Delta_M1_CI_high\": float(\n                ci_high\n            ),\n        })\n\n    return rows\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# INFORMATION / ENTANGLEMENT AUDIT\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef information_audit(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    J0: float,\n    t: float,\n    LA_values: Tuple[int, ...],\n    cfg: Config\n) -> List[Dict]:\n\n    rows = []\n\n    physical = physicality_audit(\n        V\n    )\n\n    for LA in LA_values:\n\n        if LA >= N:\n            continue\n\n        if LA > N // 2:\n            continue\n\n        A_sites = list(\n            range(LA)\n        )\n\n        I_M2 = mutual_information(\n            V,\n            N,\n            A_sites\n        )\n\n        ent = ppt_negativity(\n            V,\n            N,\n            A_sites,\n            cfg.ppt_tol\n        )\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"N\": N,\n            \"J0\": J0,\n            \"t\": t,\n            \"LA\": LA,\n\n            # M2\n            \"I_M2\": I_M2,\n            \"nu_PT_min_M2\": ent[\n                \"nu_PT_min\"\n            ],\n            \"PPT_M2\": ent[\n                \"PPT\"\n            ],\n            \"negativity_M2\": ent[\n                \"negativity\"\n            ],\n            \"log_negativity_M2\": ent[\n                \"log_negativity\"\n            ],\n\n            # M1\n            \"I_M1\": 0.0,\n            \"negativity_M1\": 0.0,\n            \"log_negativity_M1\": 0.0,\n\n            # Difference\n            \"I_difference\": I_M2,\n\n            # Physicality\n            \"nu_min_global\": physical[\n                \"nu_min\"\n            ],\n            \"physicality_gap\": physical[\n                \"physicality_gap\"\n            ],\n        })\n\n    return rows\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# FULL MI PROFILE\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef full_information_profile(\n    V: np.ndarray,\n    N: int,\n    J0: float,\n    t: float,\n    cfg: Config\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n\n    rows = []\n\n    for LA in range(\n        1,\n        N // 2 + 1\n    ):\n\n        A_sites = list(\n            range(LA)\n        )\n\n        I = mutual_information(\n            V,\n            N,\n            A_sites\n        )\n\n        ent = ppt_negativity(\n            V,\n            N,\n            A_sites,\n            cfg.ppt_tol\n        )\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"N\": N,\n            \"J0\": J0,\n            \"t\": t,\n            \"LA\": LA,\n            \"I_M2\": I,\n            \"I_M1\": 0.0,\n            \"nu_PT_min_M2\": ent[\n                \"nu_PT_min\"\n            ],\n            \"PPT_M2\": ent[\n                \"PPT\"\n            ],\n            \"negativity_M2\": ent[\n                \"negativity\"\n            ],\n            \"log_negativity_M2\": ent[\n                \"log_negativity\"\n            ],\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(\n        rows\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PROFILE DESCRIPTORS\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef profile_descriptors(\n    profile: pd.DataFrame\n) -> Dict[str, float]:\n\n    L = profile[\n        \"LA\"\n    ].to_numpy(\n        dtype=float\n    )\n\n    I = profile[\n        \"I_M2\"\n    ].to_numpy(\n        dtype=float\n    )\n\n    if np.sum(I) <= 0:\n\n        return {\n            \"xi_peak\": np.nan,\n            \"I_max\": 0.0,\n            \"xi_rms\": np.nan,\n            \"width\": np.nan,\n            \"width_over_xi\": np.nan,\n        }\n\n    idx = int(\n        np.argmax(I)\n    )\n\n    xi_peak = float(\n        L[idx]\n    )\n\n    I_max = float(\n        I[idx]\n    )\n\n    weight = np.sum(\n        I\n    )\n\n    xi_rms = float(\n        np.sqrt(\n            np.sum(\n                L ** 2 * I\n            )\n            / weight\n        )\n    )\n\n    width = float(\n        np.sqrt(\n            np.sum(\n                (L - xi_peak) ** 2\n                * I\n            )\n            / weight\n        )\n    )\n\n    return {\n        \"xi_peak\": xi_peak,\n        \"I_max\": I_max,\n        \"xi_rms\": xi_rms,\n        \"width\": width,\n        \"width_over_xi\": (\n            width / xi_peak\n            if xi_peak > 0\n            else np.nan\n        ),\n    }\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# FULL AUDIT\n# =============================================================================\n\ndef main():\n\n    cfg = CFG\n\n    os.makedirs(\n        cfg.output_dir,\n        exist_ok=True\n    )\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(\n        cfg.random_seed\n    )\n\n    print()\n    print(\"=\" * 79)\n    print(\n        \"QUANTUM-vs-CLASSICAL MEMORY AUDIT\"\n    )\n    print(\n        \"NON-STATIONARY TWO-TIME KERNEL\"\n    )\n    print(\"=\" * 79)\n\n    print()\n    print(\"MODEL\")\n    print(\"-\" * 79)\n    print(\"M2 = quantum Gaussian quench\")\n    print(\"M1 = classical separable matched-kernel process\")\n    print()\n    print(\"K0 = D\")\n    print(\"K1 = D + J0 * J_base\")\n    print(\n        \"V0 = 1/2 diag(D^(-1/2), D^(1/2))\"\n    )\n    print(\"H_Q = g^T q\")\n    print(\n        f\"hidden_site = {cfg.hidden_site}\"\n    )\n    print(\"hbar = 1\")\n    print()\n    print(\n        \"IMPORTANT: kernel is FULL TWO-TIME,\"\n    )\n    print(\n        \"Gamma_ij = <{H(t_i),H(t_j)}> / 2\"\n    )\n    print(\n        \"No Toeplitz/stationarity assumption.\"\n    )\n    print()\n    print(\n        \"Reconstructed assumption:\"\n    )\n    print(\n        \"J_base = nearest-neighbour open-chain Laplacian.\"\n    )\n    print(\"=\" * 79)\n\n    times = make_time_grid(\n        cfg\n    )\n\n    all_memory = []\n    all_information = []\n    all_descriptors = []\n\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Loop\n    # -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    for N in cfg.N_values:\n\n        print()\n        print(\"=\" * 79)\n        print(\n            f\"N = {N}\"\n        )\n        print(\"=\" * 79)\n\n        for J0 in cfg.J0_values:\n\n            print()\n            print(\"-\" * 79)\n            print(\n                f\"J0 = {J0:.8g}\"\n            )\n            print(\"-\" * 79)\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Model\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            K0, K1, J_base = make_model(\n                N,\n                J0,\n                cfg\n            )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Initial covariance\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            V0 = make_initial_covariance(\n                K0\n            )\n\n            initial_phys = physicality_audit(\n                V0\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Initial nu_min = \"\n                f\"{initial_phys['nu_min']:.12e}\"\n            )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Propagators\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            S_table = make_propagator_table(\n                K1,\n                times\n            )\n\n            Omega = symplectic_form(\n                N\n            )\n\n            # Test representative propagators\n            symplectic_residuals = []\n\n            for idx in [\n                0,\n                min(1, len(times)-1),\n                len(times)//2,\n                len(times)-1,\n            ]:\n\n                residual = symplectic_residual(\n                    S_table[idx],\n                    Omega\n                )\n\n                symplectic_residuals.append(\n                    residual\n                )\n\n            max_symp_res = max(\n                symplectic_residuals\n            )\n\n            symplectic_pass = (\n                max_symp_res\n                <= cfg.symplectic_tol\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Max symplectic residual = \"\n                f\"{max_symp_res:.6e} \"\n                f\"[{'PASS' if symplectic_pass else 'FAIL'}]\"\n            )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # FULL TWO-TIME KERNEL\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            Gamma_M2 = full_two_time_kernel(\n                V0,\n                S_table,\n                N,\n                cfg.hidden_site\n            )\n\n            # M1 has exactly the same covariance\n            Gamma_M1 = Gamma_M2.copy()\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Kernel checks\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            kernel_rmse, kernel_rel, kernel_max = (\n                relative_rmse(\n                    Gamma_M2,\n                    Gamma_M1\n                )\n            )\n\n            formula_error = validate_kernel_formula(\n                V0,\n                S_table,\n                Gamma_M2,\n                N,\n                cfg.hidden_site,\n                rng\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Full kernel RMSE = \"\n                f\"{kernel_rmse:.6e}\"\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Full kernel relative RMSE = \"\n                f\"{kernel_rel:.6e}\"\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Full kernel max abs difference = \"\n                f\"{kernel_max:.6e}\"\n            )\n\n            print(\n                \"Kernel formula validation max error = \"\n                f\"{formula_error:.6e}\"\n            )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Save kernel\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            kernel_file = os.path.join(\n                cfg.output_dir,\n                f\"two_time_kernel_N{N}_J0_{J0:.6g}.npz\"\n            )\n\n            np.savez_compressed(\n                kernel_file,\n                times=times,\n                Gamma_M2=Gamma_M2,\n                Gamma_M1=Gamma_M1,\n            )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Memory audit\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            memory_rows = memory_audit(\n                Gamma_M2,\n                cfg.dt,\n                cfg.memory_h_values,\n                rng,\n                cfg.n_classical_samples,\n                cfg.n_bootstrap\n            )\n\n            for row in memory_rows:\n\n                row[\"N\"] = N\n                row[\"J0\"] = J0\n\n                row[\n                    \"kernel_RMSE\"\n                ] = kernel_rmse\n\n                row[\n                    \"kernel_relative_RMSE\"\n                ] = kernel_rel\n\n                row[\n                    \"kernel_max_abs_difference\"\n                ] = kernel_max\n\n                row[\n                    \"kernel_formula_max_error\"\n                ] = formula_error\n\n                row[\n                    \"max_symplectic_residual\"\n                ] = max_symp_res\n\n                all_memory.append(\n                    row\n                )\n\n                print(\n                    f\"h={row['h']:4d} \"\n                    f\"V_M2={row['V_M2']:.8e} \"\n                    f\"V_M1={row['V_M1_theory']:.8e} \"\n                    f\"rel_diff=\"\n                    f\"{row['relative_variance_difference']:+.3e} \"\n                    f\"Delta_M2=\"\n                    f\"{row['Delta_M2']:+.3e} \"\n                    f\"Delta_M1=\"\n                    f\"{row['Delta_M1_theory']:+.3e} \"\n                    f\"sample=\"\n                    f\"{row['Delta_M1_sample']:+.3e}\"\n                )\n\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n            # Information and entanglement\n            # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            for t_target in (\n                cfg.information_times\n            ):\n\n                # Find nearest time-grid point.\n                idx = int(\n                    np.argmin(\n                        np.abs(\n                            times\n                            -\n                            t_target\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n\n                t_actual = float(\n                    times[idx]\n                )\n\n                S = S_table[\n                    idx\n                ]\n\n                Vt = symmetrize(\n                    S @ V0 @ S.T\n                )\n\n                # Physicality\n                phys = physicality_audit(\n                    Vt\n                )\n\n                info_rows = information_audit(\n                    Vt,\n                    N,\n                    J0,\n                    t_actual,\n                    cfg.LA_values,\n                    cfg\n                )\n\n                all_information.extend(\n                    info_rows\n                )\n\n                # Full profile\n                profile = full_information_profile(\n                    Vt,\n                    N,\n                    J0,\n                    t_actual,\n                    cfg\n                )\n\n                descriptor = profile_descriptors(\n                    profile\n                )\n\n                descriptor[\n                    \"N\"\n                ] = N\n\n                descriptor[\n                    \"J0\"\n                ] = J0\n\n                descriptor[\n                    \"t\"\n                ] = t_actual\n\n                descriptor[\n                    \"nu_min_global\"\n                ] = phys[\n                    \"nu_min\"\n                ]\n\n                all_descriptors.append(\n                    descriptor\n                )\n\n                profile_file = os.path.join(\n                    cfg.output_dir,\n                    (\n                        f\"profile_\"\n                        f\"N{N}_\"\n                        f\"J0_{J0:.6g}_\"\n                        f\"t_{t_actual:.6g}.csv\"\n                    )\n                )\n\n                profile.to_csv(\n                    profile_file,\n                    index=False\n                )\n\n                print(\n                    f\"t={t_actual:6.3f} \"\n                    f\"xi_peak=\"\n                    f\"{descriptor['xi_peak']:.3f} \"\n                    f\"Imax=\"\n                    f\"{descriptor['I_max']:.8e} \"\n                    f\"xi_rms=\"\n                    f\"{descriptor['xi_rms']:.3f} \"\n                    f\"width=\"\n                    f\"{descriptor['width']:.3f}\"\n                )\n\n                # Print entanglement summary for smallest subsystem\n                if len(info_rows) > 0:\n\n                    r0 = info_rows[0]\n\n                    print(\n                        \"    LA=\"\n                        f\"{r0['LA']} \"\n                        \"I=\"\n                        f\"{r0['I_M2']:.8e} \"\n                        \"nu_PT=\"\n                        f\"{r0['nu_PT_min_M2']:.8e} \"\n                        \"LN=\"\n                        f\"{r0['log_negativity_M2']:.8e} \"\n                        \"PPT=\"\n                        f\"{r0['PPT_M2']}\"\n                    )\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # SAVE RESULTS\n    # =========================================================================\n\n    memory_df = pd.DataFrame(\n        all_memory\n    )\n\n    information_df = pd.DataFrame(\n        all_information\n    )\n\n    descriptors_df = pd.DataFrame(\n        all_descriptors\n    )\n\n    memory_csv = os.path.join(\n        cfg.output_dir,\n        \"memory_audit_corrected.csv\"\n    )\n\n    information_csv = os.path.join(\n        cfg.output_dir,\n        \"information_entanglement_audit_corrected.csv\"\n    )\n\n    descriptors_csv = os.path.join(\n        cfg.output_dir,\n        \"information_profile_descriptors_corrected.csv\"\n    )\n\n    memory_df.to_csv(\n        memory_csv,\n        index=False\n    )\n\n    information_df.to_csv(\n        information_csv,\n        index=False\n    )\n\n    descriptors_df.to_csv(\n        descriptors_csv,\n        index=False\n    )\n\n    # =========================================================================\n    # GLOBAL SUMMARY\n    # =========================================================================\n\n    summary_file = os.path.join(\n        cfg.output_dir,\n        \"AUDIT_SUMMARY_CORRECTED.txt\"\n    )\n\n    with open(\n        summary_file,\n        \"w\",\n        encoding=\"utf-8\"\n    ) as f:\n\n        f.write(\n            \"QUANTUM-vs-CLASSICAL MEMORY AUDIT\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"NON-STATIONARY TWO-TIME KERNEL\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"=================================\\n\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"MODEL\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"-----\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"M2: quantum Gaussian quench\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"M1: classical Gaussian matched-kernel surrogate\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"K0 = D\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"K1 = D + J0 J_base\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"V0 = 1/2 diag(D^-1/2,D^1/2)\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"H_Q = g^T q\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"hbar = 1\\n\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"CRITICAL CORRECTION\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"--------------------\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"The kernel is the full non-stationary two-time covariance:\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"Gamma_ij = 1/2 <{H(t_i),H(t_j)}>\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"No Toeplitz/stationarity assumption is imposed.\\n\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"MEMORY INTERPRETATION\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"---------------------\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"M1 and M2 use the same complete two-time kernel.\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"Therefore their exact linear window variances coincide.\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"Finite M1 Monte Carlo fluctuations are sampling error only.\\n\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"ENTANGLEMENT INTERPRETATION\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"----------------------------\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"MI > 0 is bipartite correlation, not by itself proof of entanglement.\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"Gaussian entanglement requires nu_PT_min < 1/2.\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"Positive logarithmic negativity is an equivalent diagnostic here.\\n\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"OUTPUT FILES\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            \"------------\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.write(\n            f\"{memory_csv}\\n\"\n        )\n\n        f.w